From ed1e009e537c89624024183d25dd924ac732be4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:52:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Verifier custody tests: judge V26's own findings, not the
 verdict [skip ci]

Workstream 4 found that the synthetic march fixture already FAILs on
V11 (six bad placements), so the custody tests' "not PASS" assertions
held even with custody's judgement broken: custody_state around lines
314, 350 and 367 and custody_history around 436, and likewise the
custody-season and no-custody checks in custody.rs.

Each such case now compares V26's own findings exactly (code, FAIL or
not, entity, detail, transaction) and the verdict custody alone gives
(Unverifiable, or Fail with only CustodyInProgramWithoutIt). Three
mutations of the verifier that keep custody short of a FAIL but wrong (a
spurious vault-count note when lots are missing from the input, a wrong
forfeited amount, an unexplained change pinned to no transaction) pass
the old tests and fail these. Tests that generate, derive or sign keys
were not run.

[skip ci]: this branch's CI runs tests that generate and sign keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
